codex
Concrete runs now cover empty input, increasing lengths, and equal-length ties correctly. The universal proof exposed a useful issue: arithmetic could not infer that a symbolic nonempty list has nonzero length, so I replaced that check with a structural emptiness rule. I’m now shaping the loop claim as an explicit induction invariant rather than relying on arithmetic side conditions.
